# NVIDIA's driver for Swiff OS. Swiff does not ship it: the owner's host app
# (desktop/nvidia.cjs) shows NVIDIA's licence, and once the owner accepts it,
# downloads these files from Ubuntu's archive onto their games drive, under
# SwiffOS\nvidia\<version>\. At every boot swiff-nvidia.service loads them only
# if each file matches its SHA-256 here (swiff-os/NVIDIA.md).
#
#   version  the driver release, which the image's own open kernel modules
#            (Canonical's, signed) must be
#   mirror   where the files are: the archive snapshot the image is built from
#   licence  NVIDIA's licence for this release, as Ubuntu publishes it, and its
#            SHA-256: the same text the driver carries, which the owner accepts
#   file     SHA-256, size in bytes and path under the mirror, one per package
#
# The image build (mkosi.postinst.chroot, mkosi.finalize) fails if apt resolves
# NVIDIA's packages to anything else, and prints the lines it expects. Keep
# desktop/swiff-os-nvidia-driver the same (desktop/src/nvidia.test.ts).
